The four wrapper modules and installation function are adapted from that
release. Future AGI maintains changes for recursive credential redaction,
input hiding, generator lifetime/context isolation, cancellation, dynamic tools,
optional workflow metadata, and distributed parent propagation.

The upstream instrumentor still owns the single installation and teardown.
These private modules replace its wrapper implementations; they do not add
another instrumentation layer. The upstream dependency is pinned because
installation/teardown and utility APIs are private. Revalidate all adapters
before updating that pin; remove adaptations when equivalent upstream fixes
are available. No application-side helper or upstream module mutation is used.
